98346.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98346.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"This resolves #98315 by binding the method, which was not bound previously.\r\n\r\nNote; the issue specifically mentions ImageTexture as also having this problem, but when I bound both Texture2D's is_pixel_opaque() _and_ ImageTexture's, Godot threw an error, so I went with only binding Texture2D's is_pixel_opaque().\r\n\r\nI haven't checked _every_ class that derives from Texture2D, but I have checked two, and they either had their own implementations of is_pixel_opaque(), or none at all, so those _might_ be fine.\r\n\r\nI am not very confident in anything, not especially my understanding of what I'm doing here, so if I've skipped a step or caused a regression somehow, please let me know, thank you for your time :)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98346/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98346/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}